<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES- Tenders total A$169.5 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES- Tenders total A$169.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian commercial paper market saw promissory note issuance through tenders rise to A$169.6 million on Friday, the highest daily total since April 15.</p>
<p>The total was boosted by Deutsche Bank's mortgage securitisation vehicle, SABRE Securitisation Ltd, which sold A$127 million worth of its paper at between 7.03 and 7.04 percent.</p>
<p>McDonald's Corp's Australian unit made the most competitive issue on the day with its A$20 million worth of A1-plus rated 28-day paper selling at one basis point over bill.</p>
